</script>

# Message

Shows one message in a chat, with an avatar, the message text, and actions such as copy and regenerate. User messages sit on the right in a bubble, and assistant messages sit on the left as plain text. Compose it from `Message`, `MessageAvatar`, `MessageAvatarImage`, `MessageAvatarFallback`, `MessageContent`, `MessageActions`, and `MessageAction`.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Message, MessageAvatar, MessageAvatarImage, MessageAvatarFallback, MessageContent, MessageActions, MessageAction } from "#lib/components/ui/message/index.js";
	import { RotateCwIcon } from "@lucide/svelte";
</script>

<Message>
	<MessageAvatar>
		<MessageAvatarImage src="https://github.com/shadcn.png" alt="@shadcn" />
		<MessageAvatarFallback>CN</MessageAvatarFallback>
	</MessageAvatar>
	<MessageContent>How can I help you today?</MessageContent>
	<MessageActions>
		<MessageAction>
			<RotateCwIcon />
			Regenerate
		</MessageAction>
	</MessageActions>
</Message>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/message.json
```

## Anatomy

`Message` lays out its parts and sets the style, size, and radius they share. `MessageAvatar` is an `Avatar` that sits beside the content, and `MessageAvatarImage` and `MessageAvatarFallback` are the `AvatarImage` and `AvatarFallback` parts. `MessageContent` holds the text, and `MessageActions` holds a row of `MessageAction` buttons under it. The avatar and actions are optional, and the content takes the full row when there is no avatar.

## From

Set `from` to `user` or `assistant`. The default is `assistant`, which sits on the left. User messages sit on the right, put the avatar after the content, and keep their bubble narrower than the row.

<Demo section="from" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Message from="user">
	<MessageAvatar>
		<MessageAvatarFallback>AT</MessageAvatarFallback>
	</MessageAvatar>
	<MessageContent>Can you help me name a component?</MessageContent>
</Message>
```

## Variants

Set `variant` to `default`, `secondary`, `outline`, `ghost`, or `destructive` to style the content bubble. When `variant` is omitted, user messages use `secondary` and assistant messages use `ghost`, which shows plain text with no bubble. Use `destructive` for a message that failed to send.

<Demo section="variants" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Message variant="outline">
	<MessageContent>This message uses the outline variant.</MessageContent>
</Message>
```

## Sizes

Set `size` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg`. The default is `md`. The size sets the text, the bubble padding, and the gaps, and the avatar and actions use the size one step below it.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Message from="user" size="lg">
	<MessageContent>This message is size lg.</MessageContent>
</Message>
```

## Rounded

Set `rounded` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to round the bubble. The default is `pill`, which sets the radius to half the height of a one-line bubble. A short message is a pill at every size, and a longer message keeps round corners without clipping the text.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Message from="user" rounded="lg">
	<MessageContent>This bubble is rounded lg.</MessageContent>
</Message>
<Message from="user" rounded="pill">
	<MessageContent>A longer message wraps onto several lines, so the pill radius keeps round corners here instead of stretching into an oval, and none of the text is clipped.</MessageContent>
</Message>
```

## Part overrides

`MessageContent` takes its own `variant`, `size`, and `rounded`, which override the message's for that bubble only. A bubble with its own `size` in a `pill` message stays a pill at that size. `MessageAvatar` and `MessageAction` take the `Avatar` and `Button` props, so a `size` set on them replaces the one they get from the message.

<Demo section="overrides" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Message from="user">
	<MessageContent variant="outline" size="sm" rounded="sm">A smaller outlined bubble in a medium message.</MessageContent>
</Message>
<Message from="user">
	<MessageContent size="lg">A large pill in a medium message.</MessageContent>
</Message>
```

## Actions

`MessageAction` is a `ghost` `Button` with `type="button"`. Use an `icon-*` size and an `aria-label` for icon-only actions.

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<MessageActions>
	<MessageAction size="icon-sm" aria-label="Copy"><CopyIcon /></MessageAction>
	<MessageAction size="icon-sm" aria-label="Good response"><ThumbsUpIcon /></MessageAction>
</MessageActions>
```

## API

`Message` extends the native `article` attributes, `MessageContent` and `MessageActions` extend the native `div` attributes, `MessageAvatar` takes the `Avatar` props, and `MessageAction` takes the `Button` props. Extra attributes and event handlers pass through to each element.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompPropsWithChild<"article"> {
	/** Who sent the message; `user` messages sit on the right; defaults to `assistant` */
	from?: "user" | "assistant";
	/** Style of the content bubble; defaults to `secondary` for `user` and `ghost`, plain text, for `assistant` */
	variant?: "default" | "secondary" | "outline" | "ghost" | "destructive";
	/** Text, padding, and gap on the shared scale, and the avatar and action size one step below; defaults to `md` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius of the content bubble; defaults to `pill`, a pill on one line that keeps round corners on long messages without clipping */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}

type AvatarProps = AvatarRootProps;

interface ContentProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {
	/** Style of this bubble; overrides the message's `variant` */
	variant?: "default" | "secondary" | "outline" | "ghost" | "destructive";
	/** Text and padding of this bubble; overrides the message's `size` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius of this bubble; overrides the message's `rounded` */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}

interface ActionsProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {}

type ActionProps = Partial<Omit<Extract<ButtonProps, { href?: undefined }>, "href">>;
```
